<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syair Awang Semaun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Syair Awang Semaun is a traditional epic poem of Brunei recounting the deeds of the legendary hero Awang Semaun and his brothers, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-shah-of-brunei">Awang Alak Betatar</a>, remembered as the first sultan, Muhammad Shah. Preserved in oral tradition and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, it tells of the founding of Brunei and its early conquests and is regarded as the national epic of the Bruneian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malays">Malays</a>.</p></div>
